<title>USA: Central Newspapers names information chief.</title>
<headline>Central Newspapers names information chief.</headline>
<dateline>RESEARCH TRIANGLE PARK, N.C. 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Newspapers Inc (CNI) said Wednesday it named Bill Toner to the newly created position of chief information officer.</p>
<p>Toner served as director of Gannett Co Inc's Advanced Systems Lab from 1990 to 1995 and was director of technical support for Gannett Newspaper Division from 1985 to 1990.</p>
<p>Toner will begin his position at CNI on January 27, the company said. CNI said he will oversee technology issues.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
